2. Notice

The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
copies or substantial portions of the Software.

3. Attribution

This condition is a condition of the grant in section 1. Any permission granted
above is conditioned on the following being satisfied by anyone who uses,
copies, modifies, merges, publishes, distributes, sublicenses, sells, or builds
hardware from the Software or a derivative work:

   (a) They must credit the tooling that produced this work, in the form

           Built with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash running DeepSeek Harness (DSH)

       or the shorter, equivalent form

           Made with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash on DSH

   (b) The credit must be reasonably visible to the recipient of the Software or
       of the hardware built from it. Any ONE of the following is sufficient:

         - the README or the top-level documentation of the project that uses it;
         - a NOTICE, CREDITS or attribution file shipped with it;
         - an "about", "credits" or "acknowledgements" screen, page or section, if
           the project has one;
         - for a hardware design: the top-level RTL module header comments, the
           register-map or datasheet document, or the package/die documentation —
           wherever the design credits its other contributors.

   (c) The credit must name both things: the model and the harness. "DeepSeek",
       "an AI", or "automatically generated" alone does not satisfy this
       condition. Keeping the hyperlinks to
       https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 and
       https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness next to the credit
       satisfies it as well.

   (d) The credit must not be used to suggest that the copyright holders or
       DeepSeek endorse, sponsor, or take responsibility for the project that
       uses it.

4. Not required

Section 3 does not apply to: private use that is not distributed or made
available to anyone outside the organisation using it; or quoting a portion of
this Software in a discussion, review, benchmark comparison or academic work,
where citing the project is already normal practice.

5. Conditions from other licenses still apply in full

Portions of this repository are licensed differently and their terms are
unaffected by section 3 — in particular `src/hashx/hashx.c` (**LGPL-3.0**, from
tevador/hashx) and `third_party/argon2` (CC0-1.0 / Apache-2.0). See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Where a third-party license conflicts with section 3,
that licence wins for the third-party portion.

